# Scripts that get executed on Linux (bash on an EC2 instance, inside a
# Docker container, etc.) must always have LF line endings, regardless of
# this being a Windows checkout - Windows' core.autocrlf can otherwise
# silently flip them to CRLF, which is invisible in most editors and diffs
# but breaks anything that runs the script as-is. This bit a real deploy:
# user_data.sh.tpl picked up CRLF locally, making every `terraform plan`
# think the (bash-only, LF) user_data baked into the running instance had
# changed, forcing an unwanted instance replacement.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.sh.tpl text eol=lf
Dockerfile* text eol=lf
